---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="I-Beam Optimization" description="Stress analysis and Python optimization of an asymmetric wooden I-beam." currentPage="/projects">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="hero__eyebrow">Course Project · ENES220</p>
      <h1 class="hero__title">Wooden I-Beam Design &amp; Optimization</h1>
      <p class="hero__subtitle">
        Derived failure-load equations and built a Python optimizer to balance three
        failure modes for an asymmetric pine I-beam.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="padding-top:0;">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="card fade-in" style="border-left:4px solid var(--accent); margin-bottom:2.5rem;">
        <p style="margin-bottom:0.25rem;"><strong>Course:</strong> ENES220 — Mechanics of Materials</p>
        <p style="margin-bottom:0.25rem;"><strong>Team:</strong> 6 members</p>
        <p style="margin-bottom:0;"><strong>My role:</strong> Derived the governing equations and wrote the optimization code</p>
      </div>

      <img src="/images/placeholder.png" alt="I-beam design render" class="fade-in" style="width:100%; height:auto; border-radius:var(--radius-sm); margin-bottom:2rem; max-height:400px; object-fit:cover;" />

      <div class="fade-in">
        <h2>Problem</h2>
        <p>
          Design an I-beam cross-section from pine lumber and wood glue that maximizes
          load-carrying capacity. The beam has an asymmetric cross-section and can fail
          through three distinct mechanisms: flexural failure (bending stress), wood shear
          failure, and glue-joint shear failure.
        </p>

        <h2>Approach</h2>
        <p>
          I derived the stress and failure-load equations for all three failure modes from
          first principles (neutral axis location, moment of inertia, shear flow). The key
          insight was that the optimal beam should have all three failure loads as close to
          each other as possible — if one mode is much weaker than the others, material is
          wasted reinforcing modes that won't govern.
        </p>
        <p>
          I wrote a <strong>Python optimizer</strong> that parameterized the cross-section
          dimensions and iteratively searched for a geometry where the three failure loads
          were balanced within 20% of each other. The team then built the beam and tested
          it to failure in the lab.
        </p>

        <h2>Tools</h2>
        <div style="display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:0.5rem; margin-top:0.5rem;">
          <span class="card__tag">Python</span>
          <span class="card__tag">Mechanics of Materials</span>
          <span class="card__tag">Structural Analysis</span>
          <span class="card__tag">Lab Testing</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div style="margin-top:3rem;">
        <a href="/projects" class="btn btn--outline">← All Projects</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
